{"name":"Halloween","hex":"#fe653c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Halloween","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":[")","The eve of All Hallows' Day; October 31st; celebrated (mostly in English-speaking countries) by children going door-to-door in costume and soliciting candy with menaces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Halloween"}],"entries":[{"title":"Halloween","blocks":[{"text":"Halloween, also known as All Hallows' Eve, or All Saints' Eve, is a celebration observed in many countries on 31 October, the eve of the Western Christian feast of All Hallows' Day. It is at the beginning of the observance of Allhallowtide, the time in the Christian liturgical year dedicated to remembering the dead, including saints (hallows), martyrs, and all the faithful departed. In popular culture, Halloween has become a celebration of horror and is associated with the macabre and the supernatural."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Jack-o%27-Lantern_2003-10-31.jpg/330px-Jack-o%27-Lantern_2003-10-31.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halloween","wikidata":"Q251868"},{"title":"Halloween (franchise)","blocks":[{"text":"Halloween is an American slasher media franchise that consists of thirteen films, as well as novels, comic books, video games and other merchandise. All but one of the films focus on serial killer Michael Myers, who was committed to a sanitarium as a child for the murder of his sister, Judith Myers, in 1963. Fifteen years later, he escapes to stalk and kill the people of the fictional town of Haddonfield, Illinois. Michael's killings occur on the holiday of Halloween, on which all of the films primarily take place. Throughout the series various protagonists try to stop Myers including Laurie Strode and psychiatrist Dr. Samuel Loomis. The original Halloween, released in 1978, was written by John Carpenter and Debra Hill—the film's director and producer respectively. The film, itself inspired by Alfred Hitchcock's Psycho and Bob Clark's Black Christmas, is known to have inspired a long line of slasher films."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halloween_(franchise)","wikidata":"Q1364022"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Halloween_Bangladesh.jpg/500px-Halloween_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Halloween_Bangladesh.jpg/1280px-Halloween_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Halloween_Bangladesh.jpg/500px-Halloween_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalloween_Bangladesh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Halloween_Sweden.png/500px-Halloween_Sweden.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Halloween_Sweden.png/500px-Halloween_Sweden.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalloween_Sweden.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Traditional-irish-halloween-mask.jpg/500px-Traditional-irish-halloween-mask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Traditional-irish-halloween-mask.jpg/500px-Traditional-irish-halloween-mask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An early 20th-century Irish Halloween mask displayed at the Museum of Country Life in County Mayo, Ireland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATraditional-irish-halloween-mask.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Snap-Apple_Night_globalphilosophy.PNG/500px-Snap-Apple_Night_globalphilosophy.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Snap-Apple_Night_globalphilosophy.PNG/500px-Snap-Apple_Night_globalphilosophy.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snap-Apple Night, or All-Hallow Eve, painted by Daniel Maclise in 1833, shows people feasting and playing divination games on Halloween in Ireland.[123]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnap-Apple_Night_globalphilosophy.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Traditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o%27-lantern.jpg/500px-Traditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o%27-lantern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Traditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o%27-lantern.jpg/500px-Traditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o%27-lantern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A plaster cast of a traditional Irish Halloween turnip (swede, rutabaga) lantern on display in the Museum of Country Life, Ireland[143]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATraditional_Irish_halloween_Jack-o'-lantern.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Halloween_Witch_2011.JPG/500px-Halloween_Witch_2011.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Halloween_Witch_2011.JPG/1280px-Halloween_Witch_2011.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Halloween_Witch_2011.JPG/500px-Halloween_Witch_2011.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_